Song lyrics corpus — Public Release terms
(each song text keeps its own status; nothing here adds a term to a text)

Copyright (c) 2026 shani (the "Developer"), in the Developer Material only
(Section 2, CC BY 4.0). Any right in the Developer's conversions is waived
(Section 3, CC0 1.0).

These terms govern this release (the "Release"). The machine-readable status
of every file is in REUSE.toml, and the licence texts it names are in
LICENSES/.

1. SONG TEXTS. The lyric texts under songs/ (song_<n>.txt,
   song_<n>.zh-hant.txt, song_<n>.translit.txt; the "Song Texts") are not the
   Developer's work. Each keeps the status stated in its rights record
   (songs/song_<n>.rights.md) and summarised in RIGHTS_LEDGER.md:

     (a) Public-domain texts (Tier 0: song_0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11,
         12 and 13–28, with their .zh-hant.txt and .translit.txt witnesses).
         The Developer claims no copyright or other right in them and grants
         no licence, because none is needed. They are not dedicated under
         CC0 or any other instrument, since the Developer cannot dedicate
         works it does not own. For the Developer's own conversion layer in
         song_13–18 and song_26–27 (.txt), see Section 3. Notes on regimes
         outside copyright (folklore
         laws, an edition layer) are in NOTICE.md.
     (b) Dedicated and granted texts (Tier L: song_29, 30 and 31, by the
         author's public-domain dedication; song_34 and 35, by the rights
         holder's public-domain grant). No condition from this Release
         attaches to them. Attribution is given as a courtesy. The
         dedication and the grant are cited, with archived copies, in
         LICENSES/ and NOTICE.md.
     (c) Creative Commons texts (Tier L: song_32 and song_33). Licensed under
         the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International Public
         License, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
         (verbatim copy: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt), with the attribution,
         the source and the changes made stated in NOTICE.md. No additional
         or different terms are imposed on them, by this file or by anything
         else in the Release.

