3. CONVERSIONS: CC0 1.0 FOR THE DEVELOPER'S LAYER ONLY. The
   simplified-character editions made by OpenCC conversion
   (songs/song_13.txt to songs/song_18.txt) and the project's Arabic-script
   renderings of transliterated witnesses (songs/song_26.txt and
   songs/song_27.txt) are conversions of public-domain texts. To the extent
   the Developer holds any copyright or related right in a conversion, the
   Developer waives it under CC0 1.0 Universal,
   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode (verbatim
   copy: LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt). The waiver covers the Developer's
   contribution alone. The underlying words are public domain under
   Section 1(a), and they are not the Developer's to dedicate.

   The other normalisations recorded in the records' edition: fields (line
   breaks, stanza spacing, indentation, orthography) are mechanical and add
   no rights claim by the Developer to any Song Text. The normalisations of
   song_32 and song_33 are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0, as NOTICE.md states.

4. PRECEDENCE. Where these terms and a Song Text's own terms appear to
